Aerie-Purpose: Make the chrome://components status after a failed component update say that updates are disabled in Aerie, without naming Helium or pointing at the removed Helium services settings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/webui/components/components_handler.cc (ServiceStatusToString)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #131. Helium's component-updates.patch shows "Component updates are disabled. See Helium
services in settings." for a component whose update failed while Helium services are off. In Aerie
they are always off and the services page is gone (services/0006), so the text named Helium and
sent the user to a page that does not exist. The message is kept as Helium's (substitution
KEEP_MESSAGES), so this patch uses an Aerie message instead
(IDS_AERIE_COMPONENTS_SVC_STATUS_UPDATES_DISABLED, chrome/app/aerie_services_strings.grdp). Helium's
message stays in the grd, unused, to keep Helium bumps cheap. The Bench check branding_no_helium
forces a failed update before it reads chrome://components.

Depends on the Helium patch component-updates.patch (adds the lines this patch changes) and on
services/0006 (includes aerie_services_strings.grdp in the grd).

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/components/components_handler.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/components/components_handler.cc
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
       PrefService* prefs = profile->GetPrefs();
       if (prefs && !helium::ShouldAccessComponentUpdateService(*prefs)) {
         return l10n_util::GetStringUTF16(
-          IDS_COMPONENTS_SVC_STATUS_ERROR_HELIUM_SERVICES);
+          IDS_AERIE_COMPONENTS_SVC_STATUS_UPDATES_DISABLED);
       }
     }
   }
